This was my first experience working with TypeScript, although I had a very small amount of previous experience with JavaScript. Because of this, although TypeScript was somewhat new to me, the JavaScript experience helped me understand some of the basic syntax. I learned how TypeScript adds types to JavaScript, which can make code easier to understand and catch mistakes earlier. From a software engineering perspective, I think TypeScript is a good programming language because it provides more structure to JavaScript. 

For athletic software engineering, I found the WODs were defintelty better for me as a software engineer because they gave me a way to practice the concepts of TypeScript through actual coding instead of only reading about them. WODs were very stressful though because there is a very short time limit and thinking of an approach and debugging your code takes a long time, but I also think it helps improve problem solving skills and coding speed. Overall, I think this type of learning can work well for me because it gives me hands-on practice and helps me become more comfortable with programming (but maybe a bit more time would be nice).
